# Biome descriptions (2026-10-29)

BC01: Rewrite the five Create Track biome descriptions to match current terrain, lighting, road grip and creator-placeable scenery. Desert describes daylight sand rather than sunset canyons; Night describes the industrial surfaces rather than a prebuilt waterfront. Winter and Storm describe their lower-grip roads. Props are described as things the creator can add.

Changed `game/core/app.gd`, `game/tests/test_biome_selection_latency.gd`, the five rows of `scripts/translations/biomes_finish.tsv`, `game/localization/messages.pot`, and the corresponding entries in all twelve language PO files. Existing concurrent changes in these files remain outside this task.

Validation: the pinned 4.7.2 engine ran `test_biome_selection_latency.gd` headless with isolated APPDATA: 81 of 82 checks passed, including all five selected descriptions; the Garage return/shell assertion failed. A Compatibility run of `capture_create_biome_height.gd` completed 24 selections; English descriptions fit their reserved heights. Captures and layout data are in `docs/evidence/biome-copy-2026-10-29/`; the 960x540 requested window retained a 1280-wide content layout, so it is not evidence of a narrower viewport. The sandbox reported a Windows root-certificate-store error in both direct engine runs. An initial dev-wrapper attempt could not access its default user log and exited before the test; the wrapper also regenerated the client build identity. Subsequent runs used isolated local storage and the pinned executable directly.

The scoped translation check compared five authored rows with all eleven translated catalogs (55 translations) and English/template entries. `python scripts/localization.py check` reports 1481 broader existing catalog errors, including stale unrelated source entries. `python -m unittest discover -s scripts -p test_translation_authoring.py` reports four errors because the existing `track_editor_review_fixes.tsv` has a one-column first line. No phone/device test was performed. The translated strings require Godot reimport and visual acceptance; no release, deployment or owner-save change was made.
